{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, upon mut labben</b> — על מות is two words; therefore the one who says it is like על עלמות שיר is mistaken. Furthermore: why would it be followed by a lamed? Also the one who says that לבן was the name of a poet, like Ben or Yea'el, is incorrect, for it is not the way of language to say ליצחק or ליעקב with an opening lamed in a person's name, for the name is known, as I explained in the Book of the Name." "And some say: that לבן — it is an inverted lyre." "And על מות — the man of sons and the death of his son. And the correct view is that of Rabbi Dunash ha-Levi: that there was one of the princes of the nations who oppressed Israel, as will be explained in the psalm."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:42.005131976Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}